{"id": "EUVD-2026-76329", "enisaUuid": "19d53ba8-7871-38de-b60a-623aec347aff", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipmi: Remove all sysfs files on registration failure\n\nipmi_add_smi() creates the nr_users and nr_msgs files before trying to\ncreate the maintenance_mode file. If that last creation fails, the error\npath removes only nr_users before dropping the final reference to the\ninterface.\n\nRemove nr_msgs as well so no sysfs attribute embedded in the freed\ninterface remains registered.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:42:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:46:31", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d46c97eddcbc53ca885e8bb359930c58884616ff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b115b7d06f26b3f000d2afda88acb54c7a7cb2c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6c46ab0bdee90c238e96ea4a74972118c97900d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-81006", "GHSA-6fj7-8rgr-8w36"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1da98190-3d1f-3191-ba6f-426f6c61d439", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "627118470fccc61d7763aa667fcab0a9476843f6 <d46c97eddcbc53ca885e8bb359930c58884616ff"}, {"id": "2d836095-3306-39ff-8d68-9bd55bbf0cbc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.18"}, {"id": "301beb42-1c8a-37cd-9e6b-326e1dfc58da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "63081286-a68b-337d-b9c1-bf91a91ee51e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "6d74e8bc-ff5e-30bd-af88-c541399c57cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "627118470fccc61d7763aa667fcab0a9476843f6 <b6c46ab0bdee90c238e96ea4a74972118c97900d"}, {"id": "a1f569e6-af9a-3358-b3c6-e96153e2b49a", "product": {"nam